Star Schema architecture for our exercise
We'll implement the following structure.
Retail Sales Star Schema
dim_date

PK: date_id

date, month, year, quarter


dim_product

PK: product_id

name, category, brand


dim_customer

PK: customer_id

name, gender, city


dim_store

PK: store_id

name, city, state, region



fact_sales
Central Fact Table
sales_id, date_id, product_id, customer_id, store_id

quantity, unit_price, discount, total_amount

Four dimension tables connect to one central sales fact table through their keys.
4. Practical implementation using Apache Hive
We'll create five tables:
- fact_sales
- dim_date
- dim_product
- dim_customer
- dim_store
We'll use a small retail sales dataset so you can execute the practical directly in Hive.
